## Anti-AI-Slop Checklist

> [!CAUTION]
> Before submitting any UI work, verify ALL of the following:

**Colors & Palette**
- [ ] No plain red `#ff0000`, blue `#0000ff`, green `#00ff00` — use semantic tokens from this doc
- [ ] Dark mode is implemented and tested (`.dark` class toggle)
- [ ] Color contrast ratio meets WCAG AA (4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for UI elements)

**Typography**
- [ ] Geist Sans is loaded and applied via `--font-sans`
- [ ] Font sizes follow the type scale — no arbitrary `text-[17px]`
- [ ] Heading hierarchy is correct (`h1` → `h2` → `h3`, no skipping)

**Spacing & Layout**
- [ ] Spacing uses 4px-grid tokens — no arbitrary `p-[13px]`
- [ ] Layout is responsive — tested at 375px (mobile), 768px (tablet), 1280px (desktop)
- [ ] No content overflow or horizontal scroll on mobile

**Animations**
- [ ] Interactive elements have hover + active micro-animations
- [ ] Page/section transitions use Framer Motion (`fadeInUp`, `scaleIn`, or custom)
- [ ] Loading states use skeleton (not spinners alone for full-page loads)
- [ ] Animations respect `prefers-reduced-motion`

```css
/* Always include this for accessibility */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}
```

**Components**
- [ ] All interactive elements have focus-visible styles (not just hover)
- [ ] Error states are designed (not just default browser styles)
- [ ] Empty states have an icon, title, description, and (where applicable) a CTA button
- [ ] No `div` soup — semantic HTML (`section`, `article`, `nav`, `main`, `aside`)

**Code Quality**
- [ ] No inline styles (`style={{...}}`) — use Tailwind or CSS variables
- [ ] No hardcoded color values in JSX/TSX
- [ ] All components use TypeScript with proper prop types
- [ ] CVA is used for all variant-based components (not ternary class strings)

